Z||000000||Sage||10-10-2001||03:55 PM||||A couple of months ago I changed the TC lockup solenoid in my 87GT V6 automatic.  The original symptom that prompted the change was having it not shift down when coming to a stop.  I did not change the pressure switch at that time.  Should have, since it was apart and right there, but didn't, as I thought the problem was the solenoid.  It seems to have fixed the problem, as it shifts down fine now, but I notice a slight "surging" when cruising between 35-45 mph.  My question is, will the pressure switch being bad or plugged or just "dirty" cause this condition, or is there something else I should be looking at, like maybe a dirty throttle body?<P>TIA for any suggestions - solutions<P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-10-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sage:<BR><B>A couple of months ago I changed the TC lockup solenoid in my 87GT V6 automatic.  The original symptom that prompted the change was having it not shift down when coming to a stop.  I did not change the pressure switch at that time.  Should have, since it was apart and right there, but didn't, as I thought the problem was the solenoid.  It seems to have fixed the problem, as it shifts down fine now, but I notice a slight "surging" when cruising between 35-45 mph.  My question is, will the pressure switch being bad or plugged or just "dirty" cause this condition, or is there something else I should be looking at, like maybe a dirty throttle body?<P>TIA for any suggestions - solutions<P>Have a good one!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Sage!<BR>Perhaps it is the TPS causing the surge...<BR>Can't say for sure, but it has been known to cause surge...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||10-10-2001||08:20 PM||||Thanks FW, but it is very slight,kinda feels like the tranny can't make up it's mind to engage the lockup or not.  It's the surge felt after you get up to speed and the convertor gets "locked in", and the rpms drop,  but it seems to toggle back and fourth between being locked and not without the rpm change.  Wierd huh?  I will put the tps on the list of things to check out though as I do have an extra one that can be put on.  Is the tps on the 2.8 as tricky to set as it is on a 22RE Toyota motor?  (Best to have a digital volt ohm meter?)<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
